{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "We have only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 48.5% acc), leaving almost no evidence about which design axes matter most. The single highest-impact structural question is whether the image modality carries independent predictive signal. Testing config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) directly answers this while keeping profile_setting (singleprofile) matched to config_001 for a clean modality comparison. If image_only substantially outperforms rna_only, we know to prioritize image-centric and multimodal configs; if it performs similarly, the key lever becomes multimodal fusion; if both are poor, encoder choice becomes the critical variable. This experiment partitions the ~51-config search space most efficiently, reducing uncertainty about the dominant modality before committing budget to encoder or aggregation variants."
}

